## Fowler Code Smells (Reference)

The "Fowler 12 code smell baseline" used in the Standards axis of code review is derived from:

- Martin Fowler, *Refactoring: Improving the Design of Existing Code*, 2nd Edition, Chapter 3.

This is a reference vocabulary, not source code. The 12 smells are: Mysterious Name, Duplicated Code, Feature Envy, Data Clumps, Primitive Obsession, Repeated Switches, Shotgun Surgery, Divergent Change, Speculative Generality, Message Chains, Middle Man, Refused Bequest.

